<title>CANADA: SHELL CANADA TO SELL DIVISION TO PARENT.</title>
<headline>SHELL CANADA TO SELL DIVISION TO PARENT.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Canada Ltd said on Tuesday it would sell its chemicals division to a unit of its corporate parent Royal Dutch/Shell Group for C$635 million.</p>
<p>The deal, which would see an affiliate of London-based Shell International Chemicals Ltd assume a major Alberta styrene plant and isopropy alcohol facilities in Ontario, was expected to be complete by the end of 1996, Shell Canada said.</p>
<p>Shell Canada, 78-percent owned by Royal Dutch/Shell, said it expected the sale to result in a C$200-million after-tax gain.</p>
</text>
